title Donor and project components - Draft target after one-host slice 0 + project helper v1/workplace qualification; B disabled; A/C role substitutions shown
left to right direction
actor "Human donor" as Donor
actor "Project operator\nswarma-operator; no harness" as Operator
node "Donor machine\nB: separate bridge and harness UIDs\nA/C: donor UID, user service" as D {
  component "Curator init\nhuman donor UID; consent/provision request" as Init
  component "Separate donor provisioner\nprivileged B only; pending short spec/removal\nnot swarma-user-manager" as Prov
  component "Bridge service\nswarma-bridge + supervisor role\nB bridge UID; A/C donor UID\nconsumes caller-composed plan" as Bridge
  component "Harness\nB worker UID + sandbox\nC donor UID + sandbox; A donor UID only" as Harness
  component "swarma-remote-tools\nstdio relay, harness identity\nno keys / no network" as Relay
  component "Optional donor swarma-web\nown B identity / C sandbox; never harness/bridge\ntrusted-circle opt-in; pending qualification" as Web
  component "Provider proxy\nB bridge UID or system service\nC qualified proxy; A absent" as Proxy
  database "Bridge-role-owned persistent state\nkeys/config/binding/tuple/generation\naudit, cursors, budgets, queued results" as DS
  artifact "Managed home / scratch\nharness-role state; variant-owned releases\nB releases root-owned" as HS
}
node "Separate public entry host\nR-SHARED: no untrusted placements" as Entry {
  component "Join point\nservice identity unspecified in spec D9\nTLS challenge/cert/collect; no signing key" as Join
  database "Pending applications/challenges\ninvitation tombstones; signed packages" as JS
}
node "Project host\nR-SHARED: platform services only" as P {
  component "swarma-dispatcher\nservice UID; project workplace provisioning\nroot swarma-user-manager account helper" as Disp
  component "sshd (root) + relay-only stub\nfixed workplace login shell; no startup files" as Exec
  component "swarma-rb-exec\nservice principal; peer UID/generation authentication\npolicy/caps/claims/audit outside workplace UID" as Control
  component "Workplace jobs\nworkplace UID; qualified zero egress / exec profile\nUID writable set; launcher/receipt/exec.stop" as Jobs
  component "Project bridge (M3)\nservice identity unspecified in spec D5\nmailbox/admission/carrier authority" as PB
  component "Trust registry / key keeper\nservice identity unspecified in spec D4/D12\nroot/operator chain; host and separate user CA" as Keeper
  database "Project-owned persistent state\npublic worker keys/grants/revocations, KRL\nmailbox/cursors; durable effect claims + admission floors\nten-minute output cache; closed-schema service metadata\ncarrier credentials never in donor package" as PS
}
cloud "Search-provider API only" as Search
Web --> Search : donor key stays donor-side; results to donor model only
cloud "Model provider" as API
cloud "DNSSEC zone\nenvironment root/host-CA/TLS records" as DNS
Donor --> Init : only human init; policy heuristics
Init --> Prov : B absent spec/qualification -> refuse; future journal/rollback
Init --> DNS : local validation; DoH transport; mismatch/failure -> refuse
Init --> Join : Web PKI + DNSSEC default or declared no-DNSSEC invitation pins
Join --> JS : bounded queue; same-key retry recovers; other-key replay refuses
Operator --> Keeper : admission / grants / separate signed identity revoke
Operator --> Join : approve/reject; release encrypted signed package
Keeper --> PS
Disp --> PS : workplace class; v1 fw.apply + applied state at activation; no donor provisioning authority
Init --> Bridge : validated package; pin root/operator/CA, tuple and generation
Bridge --> DS
Bridge --> Harness : qualification/current policy/binding checks before exact exec
Harness --> HS
Harness --> Relay : effective tools = relay maximum intersect workplace policy
Relay --> Bridge : authenticated local socket; wrong peer/tool -> refuse
Harness --> Proxy : B/C model calls only
Proxy --> API : qualified host allowlist
Harness --> API : A direct path; no OS egress guarantee
Bridge --> Exec : one donor-originated SSH; certificates/CA/name/validity/KRL checked
Exec --> Control : relay channel only; active workplace UID/generation
Control --> Disp : admitted execution start/stop; no direct UID switch
Disp --> Jobs : root launcher / start receipt / journaled exec.stop
Control --> PS : policy/leased executions; claim identity/digest before mutation;\nreconcile same effect on reconnect; output cache separate
Control --> PB : mailbox control plane; tools only if granted
PB --> PS : durable mailbox; signatures/grants/freshness; exact-byte carrier delivery
note bottom of D
  Channel drops -> pause new turns; current deadline; channel_down; durable output queue.
  Recovery reconciles claims/floors before admission; missing/restored evidence keeps binding closed.
  Discard claims only when identities permanently inadmissible; floor persisted first.
  Retirement: account-wide absence/fence; R-TRANSFER export recorded or operator waiver;
  then key cleanup/home deletion. Retirement metadata alone has no agent content.
  Separate explicit home retention states confidentiality is not guaranteed.
  Reconnect validates trust and catches up cursors; never repeat an uncertain effect.
  B disabled until separate provisioner exists. C enforces sandbox without UID split.
  A has no OS confinement; all variants require lockdown + remote-auto and exact tuple.
end note
note right of Operator
  R-OPERATOR: phone main, displayed canonical act + biometric signature,
  pinned device-key SSH over tailnet; forced operator command, no shell.
  Terminal fallback: password sudo, timestamp_timeout=0, no NOPASSWD.
  Widening authenticates + confirms; refuses from agent session.
  Narrowing authenticates only; phone revocation: one biometric confirmation.
  Reads: mandatory swarma-observer, no confirmation. Formats/key lifecycle unpublished.
  [[../CIP-0011-credential-broker-and-agent-users.md#5-curator-broker Operator custody and act rules]]
end note
note bottom of P
  User CA private key: project keeper/hardware token; renewal only for authenticated workplace.
  OS write boundary = UID writable set; task write scope bound in plan/import.
  R-NET-TOOL: zero egress, loopback denied, no proxy; R-EXEC applies.
  Serialized per-job execution or standing runner shape/concurrency/blast radius unpublished.
  Transport/backend object ownership and closed formats unspecified in spec publication register.
  [[../CIP-0009-donor-side-deployment-and-bridge.md#recommendation CIP-0009 D0-D12]]
  [[../../protocol/remote-worker.md#publication-status Pending formats/owners]]
  [[../../protocol/remote-worker.md#tools-mailbox-and-lifecycle Recovery/lifecycle]]
end note
note bottom of Jobs
  R-TRANSFER: dispatcher materializes/exports under child UID; board resource -> exact C.
  Candidate review/rework/integration on trusted side; no worker push/MR/network.
  R-VERIFY: all heavy work/candidate execution on secret-free runners on another machine.
  R-UNTRUSTED / R-CEILINGS / R-EXEC gate admission; no subscription binding/lease.
  Standing workplace loop stays donor-side; no harness executable here (R-STANDING).
  R-WATCH: one-account freeze + journaled stop; R-ALLSTOP manual, range deny + all stops.
  Partial/unknown all-stop keeps admission closed; explicit recovery; donor channel-down.
  Default no web; task resources read-only/digested; R-RANGE-DENY / R-SOCKETS qualified.
end note
@enduml
